/F 0
/First 9291 0 R
/Last 9292 0 R
/Next 9293 0 R
/Parent 4 0 R
/Prev 9281 0 R
/Title (appropriate hardware protection. Offline payments also preclude monitoring for AML purposes. On the other hand, in comparison to traditional payment systems, the possibility for offline payments increases usability and availability of the system by allowing for instant payments, since they only need electricity to work, and still do so in the event of failures of the backend systems or of internet connection issues. Allowing offline payments thus provides a fall-back position in the case of adverse events. A convincing way to benefit from the advantages while mitigating the problems is to allow offline payments, while being subject to certain restrictions \(e. g. amount of money, number of payments, amount of time, cf. TR Backend )
>>
endobj
